Android vendored-PinMAME fixes (re-apply after ANY external.sh re-fetch of pinmame)
====================================================================================

The pinmame source under external/android-arm64-v8a/Release/pinmame/pinmame/ is NOT
tracked by git: external.sh rm -rf's and re-downloads it at the pinned SHA, silently
wiping local fixes. That already happened once (between 2026-06-14 and 2026-06-26),
regressing the segment-display fixes below ("missing segments" user reports, blank
System 80 displays). This file is the durable copy of every local fix to that tree.

Contains (against pinned pinmame 6ba56f6a8d6b5c912441e4b6b9de2cfa670591cc):
 1. src/libpinmame/libpinmame.cpp - GetSegDisplay: only read the modulated PWM buffer
    when the table opts in via options.usemodsol (mirrors core.c useDimmedSeg).
    Fixes blank System 80 BCD displays and partially-lit strobed alpha displays
    (e.g. S11 Taxi). Originally fixed 2026-06-08..10, wiped, re-applied 2026-07-19.
 2. src/libpinmame/libpinmame.cpp - tag 2-digit Gottlieb credit/match status displays
    as GTS1_4DIGIT hardware so ScoreView styles them green VFD (were UNKNOWN=amber).
 3. src/wpc/core.c - core_dmd_peek_raw_ring: read-only diagnostic accessor for the
    raw PWM sub-frame ring (offline identify-stream analysis tooling; inert).
 4. src/wpc/core.c - core_dmd_update_identify: publish rawFrameId on the recompute
    path (colour-DMD freeze fix, 2026-06-29).

History note: a 5th change (GTS3 aligned-block identify combining, 2026-07-19 morning)
was deployed once, did not fix the SMB stutter, and was REVERTED the same day - the
sliding window matches upstream vpinball/pinmame master exactly. The real SMB fix is
in the (git-tracked) Serum plugin: plugins/serum/serum.cpp [serum-scene fix] - the
plugin treated Serum_Colorize()'s return as a plain millisecond delay, but the low
word is the delay and the high bits are FLAG_RETURNED_V2_* markers; a scene-starting
match (FLAG_RETURNED_V2_SCENE=0x40000) scheduled the next Serum_Rotate() 262+ seconds
out, so scene-driven packs (smb3.cROMc: 682 trigger frames + scene generator) never
played their authored scenes. Serum_Rotate() drives scene playback internally.

Apply from the vpinball repo root:
  patch -p1 -d external/android-arm64-v8a/Release/pinmame/pinmame < patches/vendored-pinmame-android-fixes.patch

Then rebuild libpinmame (build dir already configured; do NOT run external.sh):
  make -C external/android-arm64-v8a/Release/pinmame/pinmame/build -j8
  cp <build>/libpinmame.so third-party/runtime-libs/android-arm64-v8a/
  llvm-strip --strip-unneeded -o <app>/app/src/main/jniLibs/arm64-v8a/libpinmame.so <build>/libpinmame.so
(NOTE: the pinmame build dir in the _060726 tree points at /mnt/c/vpinball-master -
 sync src edits to BOTH trees and build in C:\vpinball-master.)

